# Gotchas — arrays and casts

## The root clash

- **Arrays** — covariant + **reified** (type kept at run time)
- **Generics** — invariant + **erased** (type gone)

```java
Object[] arr = new String[3];   // covariant — legal
arr[0] = 42;                     // ArrayStoreException at RUNTIME
```

## No generic array creation

`new T[]` / `new List<String>[]` → compile error. Workarounds:

```java
T[] data = (T[]) new Object[n];   // unchecked; never expose it (what ArrayList does)
List<T> data = new ArrayList<>(); // ← usually the right answer
```

**Prefer `List<T>` over `T[]`.**

## "unchecked" & `@SafeVarargs`

- Warning = "erased cast, you're vouching" → suppress on **narrowest scope**, with a why
- Generic varargs make a hidden `T[]` (heap pollution) → mark read-only ones `@SafeVarargs`
